s which lasted three days established that Gao consisted of 7,626 blocks of houses of solid construction (clay?) not counting straw huts."<br>Timbuktu in 1580 CE<br>Timbuktu probably didn\'t have more than 15,000 inhabitants by the end of Sonni Ali\'s reign. In 1580, at the end of Askia Daoud\'s reign, it had gone over the 70,000 inhabitants mark. "Elle ne dépassait probablement guère 15 000 habitants à la fin du règne de Sonni Ali. En 1580, à la fin du règne d\'Askia Daoud, elle était passée à plus de 70 000 habitants." <br>Djenne in 1512 CE<br>In 1512, Niani still had about 60,000 inhabitants (6,000 households), as told by Leo Africanus. <br>Within the Mande-speaking heartland the basic building-block of government was the kafu, a community of anything from 1000 to 15,000 people living in or near a mud-walled town and ruled by a hereditary dynast called a fama." \n                    '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1390, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 1311})
