ds (and estimating a population of about 25-50 persons per hectare, less for the area of more scattered pottery), we estimate a population for Early I of 3,500-7,000 (Blanton 1978:33-35) and take the middle value of about 5,000 as the best estimate of population for the period. Population group continued into Late I, eventually reaching an estimated 17,000 (Blanton 1978:44)(fig. 3.4)."<br>"During Monte Alban Late I, Monte Alban tripled in size to approximately 17,000 people".<br>"Table 11.3. Population in the largest centers, by phase, in Oaxaca and Ejutla."<br>Valley of Oaxaca population (Largest center in Oaxaca): Late I: 51339 (17242).\n                    '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1311, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 1233})
